{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And she covered.</b> Transitive verb; its meaning is \"and she covered herself.\"" "<b>And she wrapped herself.</b> Its meaning is that she hid her face; likewise ויתעלף (Jonah 4:8), \"he hid his face in his garment.\" Cognate with this is מעולפת ספירים (Song of Songs 5:14)." "<b>At the opening of the eyes.</b> A place name. Some say there were two springs of water on the road, having something like an opening, and from there Judah would pass on his way back to his place."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:25.187591801Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}